**Method 6: Counting Backwards**
Start from 6 and count up to 42 in steps of 6. The numbers would be 6, 12, 18, 24, 30, 36, 42. This sequence has 7 terms, meaning each step corresponds to one child getting 6 more, totaling 7 children. Hence, 7 oranges per child, 0 remaining.

**Method 7: Number Line Method**
Imagine a number line starting at 0. Jump 6 units each time. From 0 to 6 (1st child), 6 to 12 (2nd), ..., up to 42. The jumps needed to reach 42 are 7 times. Thus, 7 oranges per child, 0 left.

