Seventh approach: Decimals and Conversion. A number multiplied by 10 is the same as moving the decimal point one place to the right. For example, 25.0 becomes 250.0. Adding a zero at the end is equivalent to shifting the decimal point, which is another way to look at multiplying by 10.

