But how do I formalize this? Maybe using modular arithmetic properties. Since 10 ≡ 1 mod 9, then 10^k ≡ 1^k = 1 mod 9 for any k. So when you expand the number into its digits, each term is digit * 10^k ≡ digit * 1 mod 9. Adding them all up gives the sum of the digits mod 9. Hence, if that sum is 0 mod 9, then the original number is 0 mod 9, hence divisible by 9. 

